2026-10-18T21:41:21.4076965Z -- v4.0.5 — one marginal COP per store, shared with the dynamics
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4077174Z   ok   marginal_cop('buffer') is the simulate step's own conversion
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4077316Z   ok   marginal_cop('dhw') is compute_cop_dhw
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4077471Z   ok   building-mass stores heat at the plain curve
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4077699Z   ok   without the Carnot derate the buffer collapses to the plain curve
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4078314Z   ok   the terminal credit repays a stored buffer kWh at the flow-derated COP the simulation charged to store it, less what the tank loses first
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4078546Z   ok   and at -5 C that haircut is small: winter storage is not discouraged
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4078767Z   ok   which is genuinely dearer than the plain curve the old code paid
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4078941Z   ok   building-mass deficits keep the plain conversion
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4079161Z   ok   derate off: the terminal term is the historical single-sum, exactly
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4079402Z   ok   a DHW deficit settles at compute_cop_dhw of its settlement temperature
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4079640Z   ok   and a buffer deficit at the flow-derated COP of its settlement ceiling
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4079648Z 
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4079942Z -- v4.0.5 — settlement caps: the lower zone's slab, a reachable tank
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4080127Z   ok   two-zone slab cap is sized from the lower zone alone
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4080490Z   ok   and it moves with the learned split, like the dynamics it settles
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4080657Z   ok   single-zone keeps the historical formula exactly
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4081058Z   ok   a strong pump's cap is the rating — mild installs are untouched
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4081311Z   ok   a weak pump against a cold day cannot reach the rating, and the cap says so
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4081527Z   ok   the reachable ceiling rises with milder weather, up to the rating
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4081539Z 
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4081808Z -- v4.0.5 — DHW conservation: a cold tank cannot pour hot water
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4081971Z   ok   the booked draw never exceeds the nominal demand
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4082152Z   ok   every step balances: in == out + losses + storage delta
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4082431Z   ok   the inlet floor fabricated nothing — the scaled draw makes it inert
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4082636Z   ok   a cold tank delivers less than the nominal demand, not the same
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4082835Z   ok   and the tank never pins to the inlet pouring imaginary heat
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4083027Z   ok   a tank at the setpoint is debited exactly the nominal draw
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4083249Z   ok   charging cannot pass the tank rating, and the excess is booked
2026-10-18T21:41:21.4083473Z   ok   a tank read above the rating cools at its physical rate, not by fiat
